@startuml AD-004-code-quality-analysis-flow
!theme plain
title Code quality analysis and refinement (UC-023) - Activity Diagram
' Rewritten 2026-10-26 (Phase 6, Task 26) to match the implementation: the platform analyses the
' generated TypeScript itself (no ESLint / SonarQube / Istanbul in the sandbox).

|DEV Agent|
start
:Write files from the LLM answer;

|System|
:Select source files (src/**, tests excluded);
fork
  :Syntax errors\n(ts.transpileModule diagnostics);
fork again
  :Complexity per function (McCabe),\nHalstead volume, maintainability index;
fork again
  :Security rules (eval, new Function, innerHTML,\ndocument.write, shell injection, secrets);
fork again
  :Layer rules on imports\n(domain <- application <- infrastructure / presentation);
end fork
:CodeQualityPolicy: score per file (100 - capped penalties),\nLOC-weighted project score, predicted QA verdict;
if (Predicted verdict = fail?\n(score < 70, syntax error or layer violation)) then (yes)
  if (CODE_QUALITY_REFINE = off?) then (no)
    |DEV Agent|
    :Rewrite the weakest files once,\nwith the findings in the prompt;
    |System|
    :Analyse the rewrite;
    if (Score higher?) then (yes)
      :Keep the rewritten files;
    else (no)
      :Keep the original files;
    endif
  endif
endif
:Write docs/code-quality.md;
:Add codeQuality to the DEV output;

|QA Agent|
:Review with the STATIC ANALYSIS section as evidence;
if (VERDICT) then (PASS)
else (FAIL)
  :DEV runs again (workflow loop);
endif

|System|
:Compare predicted and real verdicts\n(Agent Analytics: QA prediction accuracy);
stop
@enduml
